    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0885b537-c9f5-47f8-aa4f-0ad7bbebf412&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9206708040515_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Deputy Title IX Coordinator",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Deputy Title IX Coordinator Staff Full-Time President's Office, Ashland, VA, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1707 Apply Salary Range: $63,000.00 To $73,000.00 Annually Randolph-Macon College seeks applications for a full-time Deputy Title IX Coordinator. Reporting to the Director of Title IX and ADA Coordinator, this position assists with the coordination, response, investigation, and resolution of reports and complaints asserting violations of the College's Sexual and Relationship Conduct (SRC) Policy. The Deputy Title IX Coordinator serves as a primary point of contact for students, manages the intake and investigation process, prepares investigative reports, supports Title IX education and training efforts, advises College leadership on compliance matters, and serves as the Title IX Coordinator as delegated. Responsibilities: Receives and responds to reports of sex discrimination, sexual harassment, sexual assault, dating and domestic violence, stalking, retaliation, and related misconduct. Conducts initial intake meetings with students and involved parties, providing a neutral, supportive, and empathetic environment. Conducts or coordinates investigations involving allegations of sex discrimination, sexual harassment, sexual assault, dating and domestic violence, stalking, retaliation, and related misconduct. Prepares comprehensive investigation reports and related documentation. Facilitates informal resolution processes, including serving as a mediator when appropriate. Provides Title IX-related training, educational programs, and prevention initiatives for students, employees, and mandatory reporters. Coordinates and implements supportive measures for parties involved in Title IX matters. Maintains ongoing communication, case management, and follow-up with parties throughout the resolution process. Serves as a liaison between the Title IX Office and campus partners, external agencies, and other stakeholders. Maintains accurate and confidential case records in accordance with College policies and applicable laws. Promotes awareness of reporting options and works to identify and address barriers to reporting. Assists with Title IX compliance efforts, including annual reporting and required documentation. Supports the daily operations of the Title IX Office. Serves as the Title IX Coordinator as delegated. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution and a minimum of three years of related experience required; master's degree preferred or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated knowledge of and ability to interpret federal and state equal opportunity and non-discrimination laws and regulations, including Title IX, sex discrimination, sexual harassment, and related laws. Experience conducting complaint resolution, investigations, and grievance processes. Training through ATIXA or a comparable organization related to Title IX, sex discrimination, harassment, and sexual misconduct preferred. Experience with Maxient or similar case management systems preferred. Higher education experience preferred. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with diverse constituencies. Demonstrated sound judgment, objectivity, integrity, and the ability to manage highly sensitive and confidential information. Strong investigative, analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and decision-making skills, with exceptional attention to detail. Ability to manage conflict, remain calm in crisis situations, and work effectively with individuals impacted by sexual assault, intimate partner violence, stalking, and related misconduct. Ability to identify and implement supportive measures and facilitate informal resolution processes, as appropriate. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Outlook, and Excel). The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has about 1800 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capital. Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application To apply for the position, submit the following documents to https://bit.ly/4yxpeKI in Microsoft Word or PDF format: a current CV, cover letter addressing the position responsibilities and qualifications, and contact information for two professional references to Claudia Burcham, Human Resources Generalist. Screening of applications will begin immediately. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is b