    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0885b537-c9f5-47f8-aa4f-0ad7bbebf412&ccId=9200900703747_2&jobId=9207218613637_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Nursing Simulation and Skills Lab Coordinator/Debriefer",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Join Our Talent Community Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Nursing Simulation and Skills Lab Coordinator/Debriefer Nursing - Admin. Salary Staff Full-Time Nursing, Ashland, VA, US 28 days ago Requisition ID: 1726 Apply Salary Range: $64,000.00 To $69,000.00 Annually Randolph-Macon College invites applications for a 9-month Nursing Simulation and Skills Lab Coordinator/Debriefer position. Reporting to the Nursing Simulation and Skills Lab Director, this position assists with the execution of activities in the skills and simulation laboratories with specific emphasis on simulation oversight and debriefing facilitation. This is a Staff position with Faculty rank. Essential duties and responsibilities Set-up, reset and take-down of simulated clinical experiences and skills labs; facilitate simulated clinical experiences, including structured debriefings. Conduct ongoing simulation evaluation to ensure clinical currency and adherence to industry standards of best practice; assist the Simulation and Skills Lab Director with interpretation of simulation evaluation data and report compilation. Collaborate with the Simulation and Skills Lab Director and BSN faculty on simulation design and implementation. Oversee open lab skills sessions and provide instruction and support to BSN students. Coordinate lab scheduling requests from faculty and other stakeholders and maintain lab calendar. Collaborate with campus and community partners to recruit, train and retain standardized patients. Obtain and maintain BLS for Healthcare Workers instructor certification and provide training sessions for students as needed. Attend simulation-based in-service training, webinars, seminars and conferences; achieve and maintain basic professional simulation certifications (CHSE, CHSOS). Provide laboratory technical support to faculty as needed and provide laboratory tours to campus community and prospective students. Participate in campus-wide scholarship and service initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned by the Simulation and Skills Lab Director. Knowledge, skills, and abilities Ability to actively, effectively, and enthusiastically provide nursing education instruction. Experience and demonstrated knowledge of healthcare simulation hardware and software. Knowledge of simulation planning, implementation, and debriefing. Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to professionally interact and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, vendors, and campus constituents. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite or similar. Qualifications Required MSN degree from an accredited university. Unencumbered licensure as a registered nurse in the Commonwealth of Virginia or multistate licensure, Virginia eligible. Minimum of one year of clinical teaching experience. Preferred Experience and/or certification in healthcare simulation education (CHSE, CHSE-A, CHSOS, and/or CHSOS-A), or the ability to obtain such certification. The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has 1500 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capitol. Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application Please complete an online application at https://bit.ly/4rCx6r0 to include uploading a resume, letter of interest, and contact information for two professional references addressed to: Claudia Burcham, HR Generalist. Screening of applications will begin immediately. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
