    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0885b537-c9f5-47f8-aa4f-0ad7bbebf412&ccId=9200900703747_2&jobId=9206312257038_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Advancement Services",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Join Our Talent Community Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Executive Director of Advancement Services Annual Giving 110410 Staff Full-Time College Advancement, Ashland, VA, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1696 Apply Salary Range: $70,000.00 To $80,000.00 Annually Randolph-Macon College seeks a strategic, collaborative, and data-informed professional to serve as Executive Director of Advancement Services. Reporting to the Vice President of College Advancement, this position provides leadership for the operational, data, and technology functions that support fundraising, alumni relations, and engagement efforts across the College. The Executive Director oversees Advancement systems, reporting, gift administration, prospect research, and data integrity initiatives to ensure efficient operations, informed decision-making, and strong stewardship of donor and alumni information. This role supervises staff responsible for gift processing, prospect research and management, and database administration, while partnering closely with colleagues in Finance, Information Technology, and other campus departments. Responsibilities Leadership & Operations Provide strategic leadership and oversight for Advancement Services operations, promoting efficiency, innovation, and continuous improvement. Develop and implement operational strategies that support annual giving, major gifts, planned giving, and alumni engagement initiatives. Supervise, mentor, and support Advancement Services staff in a collaborative, high-performing environment. Data & Analytics Ensure the accuracy, integrity, security, and effective use of donor and alumni data. Develop reports, dashboards, and analytics to support fundraising performance tracking and strategic decision-making. Translate data into actionable insights for Advancement leadership and frontline fundraising staff. Oversee data quality initiatives and proactively resolve inconsistencies. Systems & Technology Manage Advancement systems, including CRM platforms such as Raiser’s Edge NXT and related technologies. Partner with Information Technology to support system integrations, enhancements, upgrades, and ongoing performance. Support online giving, event management systems, and end-user training. Develop and maintain process documentation, user guides, and standard operating procedures. Gift Administration & Compliance Oversee gift processing operations to ensure timely and accurate recording, receipting, and acknowledgment of contributions. Ensure compliance with IRS regulations, CASE standards, FASB/GASB guidance, and institutional policies. Reconcile Advancement records with financial data in partnership with the Business Office. Maintain and enforce gift policies, procedures, and data governance standards. Prospect Research & Management Lead prospect research and portfolio management efforts to identify and prioritize high-potential donors. Oversee wealth screening initiatives and data-driven prospect strategy development. Support fundraising staff with tools, metrics, and portfolio management resources. Collaboration & Communication Serve as a primary liaison with Finance, Information Technology, and other campus partners on data and systems initiatives. Coordinate reporting requests, system enhancements, and cross-functional operational projects. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. No less than 5 years of progressively responsible experience in advancement services, fundraising operations, or a related field. Experience with CRM systems and reporting tools; Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT experience strongly preferred. Demonstrated success documenting processes and collaborating effectively across departments. Proven leadership, project management, and team development experience. Strong analytical, organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Knowledge of fundraising operations, data governance, and compliance standards. Ability to manage multiple priorities with strong attention to detail and deadlines. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has about 1800 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capital. Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application To apply for the position, submit the following documents to https://bit.ly/4tuonXe in Microsoft Word or PDF format: a current resume, cover letter addressing the position responsibilities and qualifications, and contact information for two professional references to Claudia Burcham, Human Resources Generalist. The review and interview process will commence as strong applications are received, and the search will remain open until the position is filled. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
